1
00:00:00,279 --> 00:00:01,262
This is KiranaAI:

2
00:00:01,262 --> 00:00:04,098
agentic commerce for neighbourhood kirana stores,

3
00:00:04,098 --> 00:00:05,487
built on Beckn and ONDC.

4
00:00:05,487 --> 00:00:09,076
A family can ask for the week's groceries in plain Hinglish or

5
00:00:09,076 --> 00:00:12,606
English, and an AI agent shops across the small stores around

6
00:00:12,606 --> 00:00:14,632
them, instead of one big warehouse.

7
00:00:15,245 --> 00:00:17,278
Here is our customer's neighbourhood:

8
00:00:17,278 --> 00:00:19,915
five real kirana stores within three kilometres,

9
00:00:19,915 --> 00:00:22,718
each with its own prices, stock and delivery rules.

10
00:00:22,718 --> 00:00:24,146
Let's start the live demo.

11
00:00:24,759 --> 00:00:27,302
The demo cockpit shows both sides of the market.

12
00:00:27,302 --> 00:00:29,845
The customer talks to the assistant on the left.

13
00:00:29,845 --> 00:00:31,275
The stores live on the map.

14
00:00:31,878 --> 00:00:33,797
Our customer types one sentence:

15
00:00:33,797 --> 00:00:35,777
weekly groceries for four people,

16
00:00:35,777 --> 00:00:37,516
under fifteen hundred rupees:

17
00:00:37,516 --> 00:00:39,256
atta, toor dal, milk and tea.

18
00:00:39,866 --> 00:00:42,934
Gemini, running on Vertex AI, now works through tools.

19
00:00:42,934 --> 00:00:45,548
It searches the stores' catalogues over Beckn,

20
00:00:45,548 --> 00:00:48,390
suggests sensible quantities for a family of four,

21
00:00:48,390 --> 00:00:51,799
and runs an optimiser that picks the cheapest combination of

22
00:00:51,799 --> 00:00:54,584
stores, then fewer stores, then shorter distance.

23
00:00:55,189 --> 00:00:55,815
The result:

24
00:00:55,815 --> 00:00:58,379
one basket split across three stores, Sharma,

25
00:00:58,379 --> 00:01:01,057
Gupta and Lakshmi, with a reason on every line.

26
00:01:01,057 --> 00:01:04,190
Quantities the agent guessed are marked as suggestions,

27
00:01:04,190 --> 00:01:07,438
and the customer confirms them before anything is priced.

28
00:01:08,049 --> 00:01:11,302
Next, the platform asks each store for a verified quote.

29
00:01:11,302 --> 00:01:14,846
The total always comes from the stores, never from the model.

30
00:01:15,446 --> 00:01:17,200
And here is the key guardrail:

31
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:20,241
the agent can plan, but it can never pay or confirm.

32
00:01:20,241 --> 00:01:23,868
Only this button, pressed by the customer, approves the order.

33
00:01:23,868 --> 00:01:24,336
One tap:

34
00:01:24,336 --> 00:01:26,675
approve and pay fourteen hundred rupees.

35
00:01:27,276 --> 00:01:30,714
Payment is held, and the order splits into three store orders.

36
00:01:30,714 --> 00:01:32,045
Switching to the stores:

37
00:01:32,045 --> 00:01:35,207
all three shopkeepers get a ringing offer with the items,

38
00:01:35,207 --> 00:01:36,815
their payout and a countdown.

39
00:01:37,416 --> 00:01:39,569
Sharma General accepts straight away.

40
00:01:40,178 --> 00:01:43,820
Lakshmi Stores is out of stock, so they decline with a reason.

41
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:47,286
Within about a second, KiranaAI re-dispatches that order to

42
00:01:47,286 --> 00:01:49,754
the next best store, Annapurna Provisions.

43
00:01:50,355 --> 00:01:51,348
Annapurna accepts.

44
00:01:51,348 --> 00:01:53,776
The customer's price is locked at the quote:

45
00:01:53,776 --> 00:01:55,652
if a replacement store costs more,

46
00:01:55,652 --> 00:01:57,584
the platform covers the difference.

47
00:01:58,193 --> 00:02:00,250
Gupta Kirana simply doesn't answer.

48
00:02:00,250 --> 00:02:02,601
Shopkeepers are busy, and that's normal.

49
00:02:02,601 --> 00:02:04,423
When the offer window runs out,

50
00:02:04,423 --> 00:02:07,891
the order moves on automatically, with no one on the phone.

51
00:02:07,891 --> 00:02:11,418
Every step is a real Beckn message between our buyer app and

52
00:02:11,418 --> 00:02:12,065
seller app:

53
00:02:12,065 --> 00:02:15,592
search, select, init, confirm, and cancel with reassignment.

54
00:02:16,201 --> 00:02:19,162
Balaji Mart picks up Gupta's items and accepts.

55
00:02:19,162 --> 00:02:21,934
Again, the customer pays the original price,

56
00:02:21,934 --> 00:02:24,643
and KiranaAI covers the extra forty rupees.

57
00:02:25,248 --> 00:02:27,750
Now the stores pack and send out their orders.

58
00:02:27,750 --> 00:02:30,688
Each store moves its own order through packing, ready,

59
00:02:30,688 --> 00:02:32,374
out for delivery and delivered,

60
00:02:32,374 --> 00:02:34,441
and the customer sees every step live.

61
00:02:43,933 --> 00:02:45,675
Every store order has arrived.

62
00:02:45,675 --> 00:02:48,986
Only now is the held payment settled and paid out to each

63
00:02:48,986 --> 00:02:49,509
merchant.

64
00:02:50,109 --> 00:02:52,389
One more request, this time in Hinglish:

65
00:02:52,389 --> 00:02:54,498
two hundred and fifty grams of jeera.

66
00:02:54,498 --> 00:02:57,291
The stores only sell jeera in hundred gram packs,

67
00:02:57,291 --> 00:03:00,711
and the agent can only order whole packs from real listings.

68
00:03:00,711 --> 00:03:02,649
So instead of inventing a product,

69
00:03:02,649 --> 00:03:05,955
it explains that and offers the pack that actually exists.

70
00:03:06,562 --> 00:03:09,091
The admin ledger shows exactly who earned what:

71
00:03:09,091 --> 00:03:10,545
each merchant's net payout,

72
00:03:10,545 --> 00:03:13,613
and the forty rupee subsidy the platform paid to keep its

73
00:03:13,613 --> 00:03:14,366
price promise.

74
00:03:14,972 --> 00:03:18,225
And the audit log keeps every Beckn message and state change

75
00:03:18,225 --> 00:03:21,587
for each transaction, so every decision the system made can be

76
00:03:21,587 --> 00:03:21,966
traced.

77
00:03:22,567 --> 00:03:26,055
Under the hood, one Cloud Run service hosts the buyer app,

78
00:03:26,055 --> 00:03:27,859
the seller apps and the agent,

79
00:03:27,859 --> 00:03:31,227
and they talk to each other in Beckn messages over HTTP.

80
00:03:31,227 --> 00:03:33,753
Orders live in Postgres on Compute Engine.

81
00:03:33,753 --> 00:03:36,038
Gemini on Vertex AI plans the baskets,

82
00:03:36,038 --> 00:03:39,466
and the Gemini Live API lets customers simply speak their

83
00:03:39,466 --> 00:03:39,767
list.

84
00:03:40,381 --> 00:03:40,907
KiranaAI:

85
00:03:40,907 --> 00:03:44,359
one sentence from the customer, three neighbourhood stores,

86
00:03:44,359 --> 00:03:46,699
automatic recovery when a store says no,

87
00:03:46,699 --> 00:03:49,214
and a human always in control of the money.

88
00:03:49,214 --> 00:03:51,203
Built on Google Cloud with Gemini.

89
00:03:51,203 --> 00:03:51,788
Thank you.

